+        contract (`<class>__<method>`), the same way `self.method(...)` does.
+
+        (#49) ROUTE #189 — ONE NAME, TWO CLASSES. The walk used to `update()` every
+        nested scope into one flat map, so the LAST branch scanned won: for
+        `if flag > 0: o = D() else: o = C()` the name `o` resolved to `C`, and the
+        single call site `o.get()` was emitted as one stub carrying `C.get`'s
+        contract. MEASURED (gen #29): that file PROVED `\\result == 1` for every
+        `flag` while CPython returns 2 on the `D` branch. A name bound MORE THAN ONCE
+        in the walk is now recorded as the EMPTY class — every consumer resolves on a
+        truthy class, so such a receiver reads as UNRESOLVED and no callee contract is
+        attached. Binding-count rather than class-inequality is deliberate: it is the
+        test that needs no READ of the map's values, and this function is MIRRORED —
+        its emission types those values as `string` from the `Dict[str, str]`
+        annotation while `val.get("func", "")` is the int-typed abstract dict read,
+        and the two do not type together. The cost is completeness only: a name bound
+        twice to the SAME class also loses its contract.
+
+        The empty marker is spelled `stmt.get("__pycsl_r189_ambiguous__", "")` — a
+        `.get` of a key no IR statement carries, i.e. `""` — for the same reason: a
+        bare `""` literal would type the stored values as strings."""
         out: Dict[str, str] = {}
+        seen: Dict[str, str] = {}
         for stmt in stmts:
+            amb = stmt.get("__pycsl_r189_ambiguous__", "")
             if stmt.get("stmt") == "Assign":
                 val = stmt.get("value", {})
                 if (isinstance(val, dict) and val.get("type") == "Call" and
                         val.get("func", "") in record_types):
                     tgt = stmt.get("target", "")
                     if tgt:
-                        out[tgt] = val.get("func", "")
+                        if tgt in seen:
+                            out[tgt] = amb
+                        else:
+                            out[tgt] = val.get("func", "")
+                        seen[tgt] = amb
             for key in ("body", "orelse"):
                 if key in stmt and isinstance(stmt[key], list):
-                    out.update(IRScanner.find_record_var_classes(stmt[key], record_types))
+                    sub = IRScanner.find_record_var_classes(stmt[key], record_types)
+                    for n1 in sub:
+                        if n1 in seen:
+                            out[n1] = amb
+                        else:
+                            out[n1] = sub[n1]
+                        seen[n1] = amb
             if stmt.get("stmt") in ("While", "For"):
-                out.update(IRScanner.find_record_var_classes(stmt.get("body", []), record_types))
+                sub2 = IRScanner.find_record_var_classes(stmt.get("body", []), record_types)
+                for n2 in sub2:
+                    if n2 in seen:
+                        out[n2] = amb
+                    else:
+                        out[n2] = sub2[n2]
+                    seen[n2] = amb
             if stmt.get("stmt") == "Match":
                 for c in stmt.get("cases", []):
-                    out.update(IRScanner.find_record_var_classes(c.get("body", []), record_types))
+                    sub3 = IRScanner.find_record_var_classes(c.get("body", []), record_types)
+                    for n3 in sub3:
+                        if n3 in seen:
+                            out[n3] = amb
+                        else:
+                            out[n3] = sub3[n3]
+                        seen[n3] = amb
         return out
 
